course: dictionary
lesson: 13631
title: Words that make things happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Induce is a formal word. It means to cause something to happen, or to persuade someone to do something. Read the context: «Some medicines induce sleep.» Medicine makes you sleepy, so induce must mean cause.
explain: «Nothing could induce me to eat that!» The speaker is refusing firmly, so induce means persuade or tempt. Test it: «Nothing could persuade me to eat that!» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Science texts use induce in a special way. «Spinning a magnet in a coil induces a current.» Here it means to produce electricity without touching anything. When the context is not enough to be sure, check a dictionary.
fact: Induce is a verb. Its forms are induce, induces, induced and inducing.
fact: «Induce» means to cause something to happen, as in «Some medicines induce sleep.»
fact: «Induce» can also mean to persuade or tempt someone, as in «Nothing could induce me to eat that!»
fact: In medicine, a doctor may induce labour, which means starting the birth of a baby with medicine.
fact: In science, «induce» means to produce electricity or magnetism without touching, as in an induced current.
exercise: «Some medicines induce sleep.» What does induce mean here? | *Cause | Hide | Stop | Clean
exercise: «Nothing could induce me to eat that!» What does induce mean here? | Forget | Force open | *Persuade or tempt | Measure
exercise: «Spinning a magnet in a coil induces a current.» What does the spinning magnet produce? | Nothing, it stops the coil | *An electric current | A loud bang | A red light
test: «The teacher's kind words induced the shy girl to sing.» What does induce mean here? | Tired | Forgot | *Persuaded | Stopped
test: «Heat can induce a chemical change.» Which word is the best swap for induce? | Hide | *Cause | Wash | Prevent
exam: A doctor may induce labour. What does this mean? | *Start the birth of a baby with medicine | Stop a headache with a tablet | Weigh the baby at the hospital | Give the baby a name
